# Cataclysm 0.9 — City fights back

Implemented selected candidates **designer** and **engineer** together in `docs/preview`. Runtime and visible game version remain **0.9**. Internal patch is `42523503568-1-city-encounters`; local asset queries and visible run identity use `42523503568-1`. The `/preview/` location is unchanged. No publishing, dashboard, metadata, dependencies, frozen baseline, or other games were edited.

## Release status

**Source checks pass; browser acceptance and publishing are blocked/unverified.** The supplied `node game_factory/mobile_acceptance.cjs` could not launch Chromium: crashpad `setsockopt: Operation not permitted`, process exited with SIGTRAP. This occurred before a page loaded, so no browser/touch/layout pass is claimed. Do not publish this release until independent essential checks pass and the delivery runner verifies exact live game/dashboard bytes. No deployment, physical-phone verification, independent QA approval, or raw recording access is claimed.

The supplied base is the living-horde first-pass source, identified by its prior patch and the job's base manifest. The queue commit states that this second pass follows the verified first release; this task did not independently verify that earlier delivery. Prior source remains in Git; no rollback/frozen branch was changed. Existing BUILD_INFO files were deliberately left for the runner to stamp.

## Selected features and concrete changes

| Candidate | Source implementation | Playable impact |
| --- | --- | --- |
| designer | `game.js`: `spawnCityEncounter`, `updateCityEncounter`, `finishCityEncounter`, `renderCityEncounter`, `updateCityNotice`, elite branch in `updateEnemyBehavior`, shared `defeatEnemy`, reward pickup branch; `index.html`: accessible city notice and concise instructions | Alternating live-street hazards and elite hunts. Streets have two separated purple pools with an open navigable gap, three seconds of warning, modest periodic damage to player/enemies, and an 11-second finite end. The elite appears after a three-second location warning, aims a 1.5-second line telegraph, commits a 0.7-second dodgeable dash, then has a slow vulnerable recovery phase. It resists shots during wind-up, can be killed by existing weapons/abilities, and escapes at 21 seconds without a reward on timeout. |
| engineer | `game.js`: crane branch in the shared scheduler, `spawnCraneDebris`, `cityDamage`, `citySafeTarget`, rendering and countdown | Crane collapses warn for three seconds, then drop orange debris in a bounded alternating pattern. Each impact has another 1.6-second target warning, deals 0.65 base damage to the player and four times that to enemies, and expires after 2.1 seconds. Whole event lasts 11 seconds; new debris stop before cleanup. Subsequent crane schedule is 45–75 seconds from its start, subject to safety deferral. Followers reposition away from target circles. |

Every successful event drops one collectible ◇ rally-relay cache near the player, with a 45-second pickup lifetime and one-cache world cap. Picking it up permanently unlocks an ability interaction for that run: every companion special and rune activation leaves one radius-95 rally field for four seconds. Inside it the player is protected from the new environmental damage; enemies crossing it slow to 45% pace. This makes timing and positioning existing specials/runes useful for holding a safe position or luring enemies through debris. Repeat caches also advance companion special cooldowns by four seconds. The field replaces the previous field rather than stacking. Existing rune shield and squad mitigation also protect against environmental damage; invulnerability prevents stacked impacts. Death and enemy kill credit use actual gameplay state.

## Integration contracts

- **tick/shared time:** `tick` calls `updateCityEncounter` once using game `dt`, before updating the existing director. All event timers/fields are run state. Pause and upgrade modes stop tick; restart rebuilds all counters, schedules, rewards and fields. Minimum gate is 90 seconds and level 3, with a 180-second fallback for slow progression. Low-health (<1.5 HP), damage recovery, and frame-pressure conditions defer admission.
- **coordination:** One shared manager owns all three types. Overdue events retain their place; city types alternate street/elite while the earliest due schedule is serviced. Encounters cannot overlap each other. Start defers during the last 30 seconds before a scheduled King and while any King survives. Existing gas can coexist later; source smoke coverage checks that combination. Six seconds of recovery follow completion or elite timeout. Safety deferral can extend the nominal crane interval.
- **director:** Environmental events reserve five threat units. Elite wind-up reserves six, then its real enemy occupies those six (no double count). Admission can withdraw only distant ordinary threats, without rewards, to fit the existing budget; nearby pressure causes deferral. Normal spawns stop during elite hunts, upcoming reservation, and recovery. Budget growth, smoothing, unlock times, mutation rules, combat balance and existing caps remain intact. `director.eventThreat` and deep-copied `cityEvents` extend read-only diagnostics; existing fields remain.
- **renderWorld:** The shared renderer draws world-space circles, aim lines, debris and relay field after scenery and before actors. Crane orange, street purple, hunt pink and rally mint distinguish the patterns. Reduced motion removes falling travel; warning durations and impact targets remain visible.
- **HUD/UI:** A single pointer-transparent `role=status`, polite live region below the boss strip presents the current event and countdown, with warnings taking priority over its active-state text. It updates at displayed-second changes. Generic notices keep their existing queue for rewards and other mechanics. No extra buttons; existing action and companion rows are preserved. Short-screen instructions use smaller text. Layout positions were source-audited, but actual mobile geometry/screenshots remain blocked by Chromium.
- **companions/support:** Existing `updateSupport` buffs and tank targeting remain. `updateCompanions` uses shared event circles to move both unsafe formation targets and followers already in a target area outward. No collision walls or geometry rebuilds were introduced. All three specials and rune activation call the same relay placement hook after normal activation validation.
- **long-run bounds:** One event, one relay, one cache; at most six debris (observed three), 2.1-second debris lifetime, existing 72-enemy/180-fish/shot/particle safeguards. Unattended ordinary supplies now expire after 90 seconds and `dropPower` has a 36-item safety limit so repeated events and boss supplies do not grow forever. No earned fish/XP is discarded by this supply cap.

## Deviations and deferred work

Street hazards restrict safe space through damage zones rather than solid barricades. This preserves escape routes and avoids new pathfinding risks. Crane collapse supplies a third pattern alongside both designer city patterns. Encounters are serialized, not simultaneous; boss and low-health safety can delay nominal intervals. There is no minimap addition or new ability button. Dedicated event notices share one high-priority slot rather than entering the generic notice queue.

Researcher's rejected blackout/barricade proposal was not implemented: disabling auto-fire and introducing collision geometry were not selected. Following-cycle ideas remain full environmental geometry/pathfinding, more power-gated discoveries, and wider build/formation variety from the roadmap. Viewer suggestions remain hypotheses, not verified bugs. No new private-evidence claims are made. Natural-difficulty survival balance, physical mobile performance, all-controls-visible browser layout at 640×320 and 844×390 plus portrait, browser touch, and exact live-byte delivery remain external verification requirements.

## Commands and observed outcomes

- `node --check docs/preview/game.js` — passed after final code changes.
- `git diff --check` — passed.
- `node game_factory/mobile_acceptance.cjs` — blocked at browser launch by the environment socket restriction above; no game assertion ran. No acceptance/test source was edited.
- `node /tmp/city-qa.cjs > /tmp/city-qa-result.json` — passed. The complete source-level integration harness is embedded below so it is reviewable and reproducible without adding files outside the authorized scope. It injects test access into an in-memory copy only; production has no test setters. It stubs DOM/canvas/audio, uses fixed random seed 20261108 and 0.05-second ticks, and calls production logic. Durability, initial level 8, damage 12 and firing interval .12 are assisted fixture settings, not an unassisted player survival result. All three allies are recruited through validated upgrade selection with fixture offers. Render calls happen periodically and at each specified viewport ratio; this is not a browser CSS test or FPS benchmark.

Focused assertions cover pre-gate behavior; warning and impact timing; ordinary enemy environmental death/credit; player damage, invulnerability, shield and rally protection; ally escape destinations and real movement; cache pickup and all ability/rune hooks; elite wind-up/dash/recovery, kill reward and timeout without reward; six-second recovery; boss deferral; threat admission under a crowded fixture; enemy/debris/fish/cache bounds; delayed tier availability and mutations; upgrade/pause freezes; restart reset; keyboard and synthetic pointer movement/cancellation; resize/render at 640×320, 844×390 and 390×844; gas coexistence and frame-pressure admission suppression. Synthetic callback input is not actual mobile input.

